---

<Base
  title="Everything else I looked at"
  description="Every idea people add to a portfolio, tested inside a whole portfolio: which ones are held here, which are too close to call, which failed, and which have not been measured yet. One sentence and one number each."
  xl
>
  <Hero
    title="Everything else I looked at"
    lede="Every idea was tested inside a whole portfolio, because some ideas help on top of stocks and hurt instead of them, and the reverse. The words are explained on the about page."
  />

  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>Each card carries one of five words, <a href="/about/">defined on the about page</a>: Settled, Probably,
    Too close to call, No, or Not measured yet. Four ideas earned a place in a portfolio and are explained on
    the portfolio pages. The certain things, cheap funds, the right account and never selling in a taxable
    account, are on <a href="/how-to-hold/">how to hold it</a>. The idea behind the whole site, that stacking
    many small edges should beat the market, gets <a href="/strategies/stacking/">its own page</a>.</p>

    <p>Some ideas fail alone and help in a portfolio; some look strong alone and fail inside one. Trend
    following bought by selling stocks is too close to call at best; added on top, it gave 1.7% a year more
    growth on the same data. Cash earns the least of anything and added 0.92% back in the average worst stock
    month since 1926, for no fee. Bitcoin had the best return for its risk of anything measured and deepened the
    worst fall at every weight. Gold bought by selling stocks cost 0.4% a year; added on top it earned 0.2%;
    neither can be told from zero. So ask two questions of any idea: does it fall when stocks fall, and how am I
    paying for it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="wide mt-14">
    <VerdictGroup heading="Held in a portfolio here" count={held.length}>
      {held.map((c) => <VerdictCard {...c} more="See the portfolio" />)}
    </VerdictGroup>

    <VerdictGroup heading="Too close to call" count={close.length} gloss="The test could not tell the effect from zero.">
      {close.map((c) => <VerdictCard {...c} />)}
    </VerdictGroup>

    <VerdictGroup heading="No" count={no.length} gloss="A test written down in advance, and it failed.">
      {no.map((c) => <VerdictCard {...c} />)}
    </VerdictGroup>

    <VerdictGroup heading="Not measured yet" count={unmeasured.length} gloss="Named and priced, but no test has been run.">
      {unmeasured.map((c) => <VerdictCard {...c} more="Nearest page" />)}
    </VerdictGroup>
  </div>
</Base>
